\f1\b\fs32 \cf2 \strokec2 Task:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Design the complete motor drive control and protection logic for a high-power handheld tool (e.g., a rotary hammer), focusing specifically on user safety during instantaneous faults (jamming) and system longevity through thermal management. Your design must incorporate the following specific actions and logic:\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\li749\fi-389\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 1. Jam Protection (Inner Current Loop): Implement a fast current limiting mechanism within the inner current control loop. This mechanism must be capable of instantly clamping the armature current (Ia) to a safe maximum or commanding zero torque the moment a locked-rotor (jam) condition is detected, thereby protecting the user from severe kickback injury.\
2. Thermal Derating (Supervisory Logic): Develop a motor thermal model to estimate the winding temperature (Tw). Implement supervisory control logic that executes thermal derating\'97gradually reducing the maximum allowed speed and current limits\'97when Tw exceeds a predefined warning threshold.\
3. Fault & Restart Logic (System Integrity): Design the restart logic that locks the system into a TRIP state upon detection of a severe, sustained fault (e.g., prolonged overcurrent or critical overheating). The system must be prevented from restarting until a verifiable cooldown period has elapsed, ensuring system integrity before the next operation.\
